"""Build the six-qubit fourth-sector proof page from the checked certificate."""
from pathlib import Path
from html import escape
import json
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent

def tex(t):return '<div class="proof-equation" data-tex="'+escape(t,quote=True)+'" data-display="true"></div>'
checks=json.loads((ROOT/'independent-verification.json').read_text())
assert checks['fullPolynomialIdentityVerified'] and not checks['floatingPointUsed']
certificate=json.loads((ROOT/'sos-certificate.json').read_text())
rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{b["kind"][0]} + {b["kind"][1]}</td><td>{b["L"]}</td><td>{b["dimension"]}</td><td>Strictly positive</td></tr>' for b in checks['positivity'])
body=r'''<section class="intro"><div class="intro-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Exact rational certificate · 3 November 2026</p><h1>Six qubits:<br><em>the minimum of S₄</em></h1><p class="intro-description">A degree-eight sum-of-squares identity proves the global bound for every complex pure symmetric six-qubit state. Two inequivalent states attain equality.</p></div><div class="intro-aside"><span class="section-number">45 / 7</span><p>Proved global minimum<br>Exact arithmetic throughout verification</p><a href="../../index.html#n=6&amp;k=4&amp;mode=min">Open catalogue entry ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="reference-section" id="theorem"><h2>The sharp bound</h2><p>For every normalized state in the symmetric subspace of six qubits, the sum of squared weight-four Pauli expectations satisfies</p>'''
body+=tex(r'\boxed{S_4\ge\frac{45}{7}.}')
body+=r'''<p>Equality is attained by each of the following states, written in the normalized Dicke basis:</p>'''
body+=tex(r'\begin{aligned}|\psi_A\rangle&=\frac{\sqrt{20}|D_6^{(2)}\rangle+|D_6^{(5)}\rangle}{\sqrt{21}},\\|\psi_B\rangle&=\frac{2|D_6^{(0)}\rangle+\sqrt3|D_6^{(5)}\rangle}{\sqrt7}.\end{aligned}')
body+=r'''<p>The proof uses all seven complex Dicke amplitudes. It makes no assumption about real coefficients, sparse support or point-group symmetry.</p></section>
<section class="reference-section" id="proof"><h2>Proof by an exact sum-of-squares identity</h2><p>Allow unnormalized coefficients and set</p>'''
body+=tex(r'|\psi\rangle=\sum_{r=0}^{6}c_r|D_6^{(r)}\rangle,\qquad c_r=\sqrt{\binom6r}\,x_r,\qquad q=\sum_{r=0}^{6}\binom6r|x_r|^2.')
body+=r'''<p>Let <span data-tex="P_4(c)"></span> be the unnormalized fourth-sector polynomial, so <span data-tex="P_4(c)=q^2S_4(\psi/\sqrt q)"></span>. The rational certificate gives the polynomial identity</p>'''
body+=tex(r'\boxed{q^2\!\left(P_4-\frac{45}{7}q^2\right)=\sum_{B=1}^{18}\sum_{m=0}^{2L_B}\frac{\mathbf v_{B,m}^{\dagger}G_B\mathbf v_{B,m}}{\binom{2L_B}{m}}.}')
body+=r'''<p>Each component of <span data-tex="\mathbf v_{B,m}(x,\bar x)"></span> is a homogeneous polynomial of degree four with rational coefficients. Every <span data-tex="G_B"></span> is a real symmetric positive-definite rational matrix. Their entries and the polynomial components are explicitly supplied in <a href="sos-certificate.json" download>the Gram certificate</a> and <a href="basis.json" download>the polynomial basis</a>.</p><p>The right-hand side is nonnegative for arbitrary complex amplitudes. Dividing by <span data-tex="q^4&gt;0"></span> proves the inequality for every nonzero state. The exact equality states complete the optimality proof.</p><p>The identity was checked coefficient by coefficient, treating the amplitudes and their conjugates as independent variables. The target polynomial was independently derived from reduced Dicke density matrices. Positivity was checked by exact rational leading principal minors, separately from the certificate producer’s exact LDL decomposition. No optimizer output or floating-point tolerance enters the verification.</p>'''
body+=f'''<details><summary>Certificate size and positivity checks</summary><p>The coefficient comparison checks all {certificate['identityMonomialsChecked']} monomials occurring before cancellation; {checks['nonzeroDegreeEightMonomials']} have nonzero target coefficients. The {checks['positiveDefiniteGramBlocks']} Gram blocks have size at most seven. Exact LDL decomposition rewrites the identity as {checks['squaredForms']} positively weighted absolute squares.</p><table class="gap-table"><thead><tr><th>Amplitude + conjugate degree</th><th>Spin L</th><th>Matrix size</th><th>Leading principal minors</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}</tbody></table><p><a href="independent-verification.json" download>All exact positivity minors and file hashes ↓</a></p></details>'''
body+=r'''<details><summary>Reduced-density-matrix derivation of the target</summary><p>In binomial-scaled coordinates the unnormalized reduction is</p>'''
body+=tex(r'(\rho_t)_{ab}=\sqrt{\binom ta\binom tb}\sum_{j=0}^{6-t}\binom{6-t}{j}x_{a+j}\overline{x_{b+j}}.')
body+=tex(r'P_4=15\sum_{t=0}^{4}(-1)^{4-t}\binom4t2^t\operatorname{tr}(\rho_t^2).')
body+=r'''<p>This purity inversion directly gives the polynomial used on the left of the certificate. The verifier rebuilds it independently, without spin-coupling or optimization routines. <a href="target-exact.json" download>Expanded target polynomial ↓</a></p></details>
<details><summary>Reading the exact certificate</summary><p>In <code>basis.json</code>, indices 0–6 denote the seven variables <span data-tex="x_0,\ldots,x_6"></span>, and indices 7–13 denote their complex conjugates. A sorted list of four indices specifies a degree-four monomial, followed by its integer coefficient. Divide each basis channel by the corresponding rational factor in <code>basisScales</code> before applying its Gram matrix. The magnetic-component weights are exactly the reciprocal binomial coefficients displayed above. These conventions completely specify the identity.</p><p>The optional <a href="build_basis.py">basis generator</a> derives the covariants by binary-form transvectants and imposes the two equality states. The proof verifier needs only the explicit basis and matrix data; it does not assume that this discovery procedure was complete.</p></details></section>
<section class="reference-section" id="equality"><h2>Equality states and a paired family</h2><p>The two states above have identical full sector vectors:</p>'''
body+=tex(r'(S_0,\ldots,S_6)=\left(1,\frac{24}{49},\frac{405}{49},\frac{440}{49},\frac{45}{7},\frac{1104}{49},\frac{799}{49}\right).')
body+=r'''<p>Nevertheless they are inequivalent: their Majorana multiplicity patterns are <span data-tex="(2,1^4)"></span> and <span data-tex="(1^6)"></span>. Collective rotations and invertible collective SLOCC transformations preserve multiplicities. Their proper rotational symmetry groups are <span data-tex="C_3"></span> and <span data-tex="C_5"></span>, respectively.</p><p>More generally, for <span data-tex="0\le p\le1"></span>, define</p>'''
body+=tex(r'\begin{aligned}|A(p)\rangle&=\sqrt p\,|D_6^{(2)}\rangle+\sqrt{1-p}\,|D_6^{(5)}\rangle,\\|B(p)\rangle&=\sqrt{\frac{3p}{5}}\,|D_6^{(0)}\rangle+\sqrt{1-\frac{3p}{5}}\,|D_6^{(5)}\rangle.\end{aligned}')
body+=r'''<p>All seven sector lengths of these two families agree. In particular,</p>'''
body+=tex(r'S_4(A(p))=S_4(B(p))=\frac{45}{7}+\frac{84}{5}\left(p-\frac{20}{21}\right)^2.')
body+=r'''<p>This square completion proves equality at the stated states; the separate global certificate rules out smaller values anywhere else. Relative phases in each two-component family can be removed by a collective rotation about the z axis. <a href="two_component_families.py">Exact family verifier</a> · <a href="two-component-families.json" download>All sector polynomials ↓</a></p></section>
<section class="reference-section" id="moments"><h2>Equivalent sharp spin-moment inequality</h2><p>Use spin three with <span data-tex="J_z|D_6^{(r)}\rangle=(3-r)|D_6^{(r)}\rangle"></span>, and normalized states. Define</p>'''
body+=tex(r'F_i=\langle J_i\rangle,\quad \mathsf Q_{ij}=\left\langle\frac{J_iJ_j+J_jJ_i}{2}\right\rangle-4\delta_{ij},\quad\theta=\sum_{r=0}^{6}(-1)^r c_rc_{6-r}.')
body+=tex(r'S_4=11+\frac83|\mathbf F|^2-\frac8{15}\operatorname{tr}(\mathsf Q^2)+24|\theta|^2.')
body+=r'''<p>The proved bound is therefore equivalent to</p>'''
body+=tex(r'\boxed{\operatorname{tr}(\mathsf Q^2)\le\frac{60}{7}+5|\mathbf F|^2+45|\theta|^2.}')
body+=r'''<h3>Necessary and sufficient conditions for equality</h3><p>The scalar block of the certificate gives the following exact characterization for normalized states:</p>'''
body+=tex(r'S_4=\frac{45}{7}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\theta=0,\quad |\mathbf F|^2=\frac{36}{49},\quad\operatorname{tr}(\mathsf Q^2)=\frac{600}{49}.')
body+=r'''<p>At equality every positive summand vanishes. The three scalar covariants are proportional, by nonzero rational factors, to the following expressions:</p>'''
body+=tex(r'\begin{aligned}h_1&=\frac14|\theta|^2,\\h_2&=-3-\frac{11}{12}|\mathbf F|^2-5|\theta|^2+\frac3{10}\operatorname{tr}(\mathsf Q^2),\\h_3&=\frac{49}{5}-\frac{1309}{20}|\mathbf F|^2-\frac{769}{5}|\theta|^2+\frac{469}{150}\operatorname{tr}(\mathsf Q^2).\end{aligned}')
body+=r'''<p>Solving these three independent linear equations gives the stated values. Conversely, substituting these values in the exact spin-moment identity gives equality. This characterizes the moments of every minimizer; it does not classify all minimizing states up to rotations. <a href="verify_equality_conditions.py">Exact equality-condition verifier</a> · <a href="equality-verification.json">Verification record</a></p>'''
body+=r'''<p>The spin-moment identity was independently checked against every reduced-purity polynomial coefficient. <a href="verify_spin_moments.py">Exact check</a> · <a href="spin-moment-check.json">Verification record</a></p></section>
<section class="reference-section" id="verify"><h2>Reproduce the proof</h2><p>From this research directory, run the following with ordinary Python 3. The global verifier uses only the standard library and exact rational arithmetic.</p><pre class="precision">python3 verify_certificate.py</pre><p>For the supplementary family and spin-moment identities, with SymPy installed:</p><pre class="precision">python3 two_component_families.py
python3 verify_spin_moments.py</pre><p><a href="verify_certificate.py">Read the standalone proof verifier</a> · <a href="independent-verification.json" download>Verification report ↓</a> · <a href="sos-certificate.json" download>Rational certificate ↓</a> · <a href="basis.json" download>Explicit quartic polynomials ↓</a></p><p>Numerical semidefinite optimization was used to discover a suitable matrix decomposition. After rational reconstruction, every polynomial coefficient and every positive principal minor was checked exactly. This is a computer-assisted algebraic proof, rather than numerical evidence for a bound.</p></section>
<section class="reference-section" id="context"><h2>Relation to spin-three condensates</h2><p>The paired threefold and fivefold families occur in the spin-three Bose–Einstein-condensate literature, where rotationally invariant quartic energies share the same degeneracy. See <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/0611230">Barnett, Turner and Demler (2007)</a> and <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1109.0400">Kawaguchi and Ueda (2011)</a>. Their phase classification motivates the equality states. The universal fourth-sector lower bound here is established independently by the exact polynomial certificate.</p></section>'''
html=r'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Six-qubit S₄ minimum · Exact proof</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js" defer></script><style>.proof-equation{overflow-x:auto;margin:1.4rem 0;padding:.4rem 0}.precision{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;background:var(--panel,#f0f1eb);padding:1rem}details{margin:1.4rem 0}summary{cursor:pointer}.research-page main{max-width:1100px}.gap-table{margin:1.4rem 0}</style></head><body class="research-page"><header class="site-header"><a class="wordmark" href="../../index.html#n=6&amp;k=4&amp;mode=min">← Sector-length catalogue</a><nav aria-label="Proof navigation"><a href="#theorem">Theorem</a><a href="#proof">Proof</a><a href="#equality">Equality</a><a href="#verify">Verify</a></nav></header><main>'''+body+'''</main><footer class="site-footer"><p>Extremal symmetric states</p><a href="../index.html">All proofs and remaining gaps ↗</a></footer><script>document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',()=>document.querySelectorAll('[data-tex]').forEach(el=>{el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:el.dataset.display==='true',throwOnError:false,trust:false})}));</script></body></html>'''
# All inline mathematical commands are literal LaTeX; guard control-character escapes.
for char in ['\x08','\x0c','\x0b']:
 assert char not in html,repr(char)
(ROOT/'index.html').write_text(html)
print('Built six-qubit S4 theorem, exact certificate and equality-state page.')
